== 3. FINDING A (blocking) — behaviour 5's refusal evidence does not bite ==
Five synthetic-manifest refusal fixtures in packages/commands/src/delegate.test.ts.
assertRefused (delegate.test.ts:~168) asserts only exitCode !== 0 + unchanged bytes;
it never asserts WHICH refusal fired. Measured, one fixture at a time:
  :189 5-parse-error  claims delegate.ts:139  -> actually 'unparseable — not a studio' (openStudio, delegate.ts:113)
  :194 5-dup-key      claims delegate.ts:139  -> actually 'Map keys must be unique' (openStudio)
  :199 5-multi-doc    claims delegate.ts:134  -> actually 'Source contains multiple documents' (openStudio)
  :204 5-merge-key    claims hasMergeKey :147 -> actually the anchor/alias scan :143 (fixture uses &def/*def)
  :214 5-anchor-alias claims :143 — with :143 disabled it still exits 2, via a CRASH:
        "delegate failed: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'toLowerCase')"
Consequences:
  - delegate.ts:134-137 (multi-document) and delegate.ts:51-60/147-150 (hasMergeKey) are
    UNREACHABLE by any test: openStudio parses first with the same library and rejects
    every document-level malformation before the whitelist is consulted.
  - the brief's own mutant 'Narrow the anchor/alias check back to alias-on-the-path' SURVIVES.
Root cause is one helper: assertRefused takes no expected-message argument.

