== 14. verdict ==
FAIL, round 1. Gates are green and the feature works end to end; the failure is EVIDENCE.
Findings A, B and C are blocking and all three lie inside W-065's own files:
  A behaviour 5's refusals pass for the wrong reason (5 fixtures), leaving two shipped
    code paths unreachable by any test. One fix: give assertRefused an expected-message arg.
  B four of the brief's own mutants survive, one shape: assertions pin only the lower bound.
  C behaviour 3's harnessVersions clause is unimplemented, unasserted and mis-disclosed as
    'deferred to the server' when the server does not implement it either.
Findings D and E are advisory and should be filed, not fixed under this gate — D needs a
stop-and-ask on the workflow.* name (or the one-line drop of the emit), E is a limit of a
single writeFileSync with no seam.
